        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-ta" value="Option A — HF-resident input&#10;Candidate: Kafka Messaging Modular Input v1.9.0 (BaboonBones; Developer Supported). Splunkbase lists Enterprise 10.0–10.7 and forwarder installation. Consumer-group, framing, and large-message behavior require validation for the exact add-on." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=18;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="665" width="750" height="155" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-soc4kafka" value="Option B — Splunk OTel Collector for Kafka (SOC4Kafka)&#10;Replacement for Splunk Connect for Kafka, whose EOL is 2027-10-31. Configure Kafka receiver → HEC exporter; leave processors empty and send to HF HEC to preserve HF/EP processing. README lists Kafka 3.7+, Splunk 9.x+, and no acknowledgment or Protobuf support." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=18;fillColor=#DDEBF7;strokeColor=#4472C4;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="850" y="665" width="750" height="155" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="footer" value="Logical configuration domains (including Kafka): A = 6 (5 Splunk-side); B = 6 (5 Splunk-side). Count is by management domain, not files or machines. Size/throughput require end-to-end testing. Splunk deployment and Kafka icons are embedded; EP and SOC4Kafka use standard shapes." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#555555;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="870" width="1530" height="45" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
